UPDATE goods_relationships SET framing = '{"slug":"snow-foundation","tone":"values-driven, community-respectful","framing_notes":"Active multi-tranche partner. Xero shows $402,930 received + $132,000 AUTHORISED across 7 tranches over 14 months (INV-0321 $132K currently outstanding 37d). No single canonical ask — relationship funds in rolling tranches on project ACT-GD. Last comm 10 days ago, warm. Next action (only-Ben): call Sally or Alexandra to confirm INV-0321 payment AND flag Pty migration — from 1 July 2026 tranches invoice to A Curious Tractor Pty Ltd ACN 697 347 676. Tour funder sponsorship candidate. Lead with the closed-loop framing and the regional / Indigenous-led work.","claims_to_lead_with":["empathy-ledger:claim-the-loop-is-the-product","contained:claim-room-3-community-already-doing-it","goods-on-country:claim-not-charity-its-enterprise"],"claims_to_avoid":[],"primary_contact":"Sally Grimsley-Ballard / Alexandra Lagelee Kean","last_communicated_at":"2026-05-20","synced_at":"2026-06-10T00:40:49.288Z"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE id = '69f42a07-ccf4-4c8d-bff6-35177d9bd62f';
UPDATE goods_relationships SET framing = '{"slug":"mrff-uom-palmer","tone":"research-partnership, sovereignty-first, evidence-grounded","framing_notes":"Grant AWARDED (Mental Health and Climate Change 2026-2031); Year 1 = Getting to Know You Year (Mar 2026 to Mar 2027), running now. The negotiation opening is the E2 in-kind pledge: Moments in Communities, value to be determined. Five-year ACT envelope target roughly 450k-750k AUD, of which a contractually protected share is community payments. Pitch decision #3 (editor role) settles with Nick before the Palmer conversation. Decision #4 REFRAMED (Ben, 7 Jun 2026): the storyteller payment rate is co-designed WITH each community as an ongoing process, never pre-set in Brisbane; what settles with Nick beforehand is the floor principle (a protected minimum) plus the one-person-one-rate rule (identical across Goods and grant lanes). Pitch the mechanism, not a number: community-set rates with a contractual floor. Deadline targets landing the Palmer conversation before relay departure 27 Jun. The relay tour through Tennant Creek IS Year 1 engagement for a grant-named site, captured before any grant dollar is invoiced. Sources: thoughts/shared/proposals/2026-06-05-mrff-five-year-partnership-plan.md + 2026-06-05-mrff-climate-mental-health-el-goods-alignment.md (empathy-ledger-v2 repo).","claims_to_lead_with":["ACT is named in the funded grant text: Partner AIs for Tennant Creek + Palm Island; partners A Curious Tractor will develop the interactive map (milestone Mar 2027 to Sept 2028)","The story system already exists and is proven: consent-gated relay trails, publish/media gates, the scrollytelling journey map on Empathy Ledger","Community payment floor as contractual headline: a fixed share of every ACT invoice flows to community participants, reported through the platform itself"],"claims_to_avoid":["Beds or freight as grant lines (they stay in the Centrecorp/Snow lane; the grant pays for the story system only)","Any community payment claim not backed by the visible payment schedule","In-kind goods counted as storyteller payment (one cash rate per ledger unit, identical Goods-side and grant-side)"],"primary_contact":"Prof Victoria Palmer (CIA, UoM / ALIVE National Centre)","last_communicated_at":null,"synced_at":"2026-06-10T00:40:49.288Z"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE id = '62fdf486-adb4-4683-be08-9f2d781b7ae6';
